---Specifies the properties of a managed disk that can be set at the time of implicit creation of the disk.
---@class azure.compute.ManagedDiskProperties
---@field tier? string Performance tier of the disk (e.g., P4, S10) as described here: https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/pricing/details/managed-disks/. Does not apply to Ultra disks.
---@field burstingEnabled? boolean Set to true to enable bursting beyond the provisioned performance target of the disk. Bursting is disabled by default. Does not apply to Ultra disks.
---@field performancePlus? boolean Set this flag to true to get a boost on the performance target of the disk deployed. This flag can only be set on disk creation time and cannot be disabled after enabled.
---@field optimizedForFrequentAttach? boolean Setting this property to true improves reliability and performance of data disks that are frequently (more than 5 times a day) detached from one virtual machine and attached to another. This property should not be set for disks that are not detached and attached frequently as it causes the disks to not align with the fault domain of the virtual machine.
---@field availabilityPolicy? azure.compute.DiskAvailabilityPolicy In the case of an availability or connectivity issue with the disk, specify the behavior of your VM.
---@field maxShares? number The maximum number of VMs that can attach to the disk at the same time. Value greater than one indicates a disk that can be mounted on multiple VMs at the same time. Applies to data disks only.
---@field networkAccessPolicy? azure.compute.NetworkAccessPolicy|string Policy for accessing the disk via network.
---@field diskAccessId? string Azure resource Id of the DiskAccess resource for using private endpoints on disks.
---@field diskIOPSReadOnly? number The total number of IOPS that will be allowed across all VMs mounting the shared disk as ReadOnly. One operation can transfer between 4k and 256k bytes.
---@field diskMBpsReadOnly? number The total throughput (MBps) that will be allowed across all VMs mounting the shared disk as ReadOnly. MBps means millions of bytes per second - MB here uses the ISO notation, of powers of 10.
---@field logicalSectorSize? number Logical sector size in bytes for Ultra Disks. Supported values are 512 and 4096. 4096 is the default.

