---Describes the properties of a Virtual Machine.
---@class azure.compute.VirtualMachineProperties
---@field hardwareProfile? azure.compute.HardwareProfile Specifies the hardware settings for the virtual machine.
---@field flexProfile? azure.compute.FlexProfile [Preview Feature] Specifies a FlexProfile for VM size. Azure may deploy a compatible alternative VM size based on capacity and placement considerations, and returns the deployed size in hardwareProfile.vmSize. A request that adds flexProfile must omit hardwareProfile.vmSize. For a virtual machine that uses FlexProfile, a hardwareProfile.vmSize equal to the deployed size is ignored, so a GET response can be sent back unchanged. A PATCH request that omits flexProfile keeps it. A PUT request that omits flexProfile and sets hardwareProfile.vmSize clears it. This property cannot exist along with a non-null properties.availabilitySet, properties.capacityReservation, properties.host, properties.hostGroup, properties.proximityPlacementGroup or properties.virtualMachineScaleSet.
---@field scheduledEventsPolicy? azure.compute.ScheduledEventsPolicy Specifies Redeploy, Reboot and ScheduledEventsAdditionalPublishingTargets Scheduled Event related configurations for the virtual machine.
---@field storageProfile? azure.compute.StorageProfile Specifies the storage settings for the virtual machine disks.
---@field additionalCapabilities? azure.compute.AdditionalCapabilities Specifies additional capabilities enabled or disabled on the virtual machine.
---@field osProfile? azure.compute.OSProfile Specifies the operating system settings used while creating the virtual machine. Some of the settings cannot be changed once VM is provisioned.
---@field networkProfile? azure.compute.NetworkProfile Specifies the network interfaces of the virtual machine.
---@field securityProfile? azure.compute.SecurityProfile Specifies the Security related profile settings for the virtual machine.
---@field diagnosticsProfile? azure.compute.DiagnosticsProfile Specifies the boot diagnostic settings state. Minimum api-version: 2015-06-15.
---@field availabilitySet? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePropertiesAvailabilitySet
---@field virtualMachineScaleSet? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePropertiesVirtualMachineScaleSet
---@field proximityPlacementGroup? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePropertiesProximityPlacementGroup
---@field priority? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePriorityTypes Specifies the priority for the virtual machine. Minimum api-version: 2019-03-01
---@field evictionPolicy? azure.compute.VirtualMachineEvictionPolicyTypes Specifies the eviction policy for the Azure Spot virtual machine and Azure Spot scale set. For Azure Spot virtual machines, both 'Deallocate' and 'Delete' are supported and the minimum api-version is 2019-03-01. For Azure Spot scale sets, both 'Deallocate' and 'Delete' are supported and the minimum api-version is 2017-10-30-preview.
---@field billingProfile? azure.compute.BillingProfile Specifies the billing related details of a Azure Spot virtual machine. Minimum api-version: 2019-03-01.
---@field host? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePropertiesHost
---@field hostGroup? azure.compute.VirtualMachinePropertiesHostGroup
---@field provisioningState? string The provisioning state, which only appears in the response.
---@field instanceView? azure.compute.VirtualMachineInstanceView The virtual machine instance view.
---@field licenseType? string Specifies that the image or disk that is being used was licensed on-premises. <br><br> Possible values for Windows Server operating system are: <br><br> Windows_Client <br><br> Windows_Server <br><br> Possible values for Linux Server operating system are: <br><br> RHEL_BYOS (for RHEL) <br><br> SLES_BYOS (for SUSE) <br><br> For more information, see [Azure Hybrid Use Benefit for Windows Server](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/windows/hybrid-use-benefit-licensing) <br><br> [Azure Hybrid Use Benefit for Linux Server](https://docs.microsoft.com/azure/virtual-machines/linux/azure-hybrid-benefit-linux) <br><br> Minimum api-version: 2015-06-15
---@field vmId? string Specifies the VM unique ID which is a 128-bits identifier that is encoded and stored in all Azure IaaS VMs SMBIOS and can be read using platform BIOS commands.
---@field extensionsTimeBudget? string Specifies the time alloted for all extensions to start. The time duration should be between 15 minutes and 120 minutes (inclusive) and should be specified in ISO 8601 format. The default value is 90 minutes (PT1H30M). Minimum api-version: 2020-06-01.
---@field platformFaultDomain? number Specifies the scale set logical fault domain into which the Virtual Machine will be created. By default, the Virtual Machine will by automatically assigned to a fault domain that best maintains balance across available fault domains. This is applicable only if the 'virtualMachineScaleSet' property of this Virtual Machine is set. The Virtual Machine Scale Set that is referenced, must have 'platformFaultDomainCount' greater than 1. This property cannot be updated once the Virtual Machine is created. Fault domain assignment can be viewed in the Virtual Machine Instance View. Minimum api‐version: 2020‐12‐01.
---@field scheduledEventsProfile? azure.compute.ScheduledEventsProfile Specifies Scheduled Event related configurations.
---@field userData? string UserData for the VM, which must be base-64 encoded. Customer should not pass any secrets in here. Minimum api-version: 2021-03-01.
---@field capacityReservation? azure.compute.CapacityReservationProfile Specifies information about the capacity reservation that is used to allocate virtual machine. Minimum api-version: 2021-04-01.
---@field interconnectBlockProfile? azure.compute.InterconnectBlockProfile Specifies information about the Interconnect Block that is used to allocate the Virtual Machine. Minimum api-version: 2026-03-01.
---@field applicationProfile? azure.compute.ApplicationProfile Specifies the gallery applications that should be made available to the VM/VMSS.
---@field timeCreated? string Specifies the time at which the Virtual Machine resource was created. Minimum api-version: 2021-11-01.
---@field resiliencyProfile? azure.compute.ResiliencyProfile Resiliency profile for the virtual machine.

